# WebSocket commands — use a WS client connected to:
# ws://{{host}}/ws?token={{authToken}}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/ws
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  ## The Record button over the WebSocket

  ### Commands (token required)

  ```json
  { "type": "recorders.start" }
  { "type": "recorders.stop" }
  ```

  Each starts or stops every recorder in `GET /api/settings/record-button`, side by side, through
  the same code automations use: one already recording is left alone. The answer is `ok`, or
  `{ "type": "error", "message": "recorders_failed: blackmagic-camera: camera_no_media; obs: obs_not_connected" }`.

  ### Broadcasts

  ```json
  {
    "type": "recorders.state",
    "recorders": [
      { "target": { "device": "blackmagic-camera" }, "selected": true, "available": true, "recording": false,
        "lastStart": { "at": "2026-10-26T09:00:00Z", "error": "camera_no_media" } },
      { "target": { "device": "rodecaster-audio" }, "selected": true, "available": true, "recording": true,
        "lastStart": { "at": "2026-10-26T09:00:00Z", "error": null } }
    ]
  }
  { "type": "recorder.stopped", "target": { "device": "blackmagic-camera" }, "reason": "device", "error": "camera_no_media" }
  ```

  `recorders.state` goes out when any row changes. `recorder.stopped` goes out whenever any
  recording stops, selected or not. `reason` is `metocast` (the Record button, a Live page button
  or an automation), `disconnected` (the connection dropped) or `device` (it stopped by itself, or
  someone stopped it on the device).
}
